# features.list — what you can add to Vikix, and remove again:
#   vikix add NAME, vikix remove NAME, vikix features
#
# One feature a line, fields split by |:
#   name     what you type
#   lists    its package lists in packages/ (optional/ ones with the prefix)
#   needs    other features it brings along
#   add      a command that sets it up instead of just its lists (it records
#            the feature itself, through vikix-features record)
#   remove   a command to run before its packages go (it asks, if it deletes
#            anything of yours)
#   about    one line, for vikix features and the welcome
#
# A package list that no feature names is part of the base: install.sh
# installs it and every update keeps it. So a new list is for everyone
# until a line here makes it a choice.
#
# Your choices are ~/.config/vikix/features (lib/features.sh reads them).
# Bundles of features, such as essentials, are in bundles.list.

# name      | lists              | needs    | add                 | remove                | about
emacs       | emacs editor-tools |          |                     |                       | Emacs, with Vikix's config; SLIME reaches the running window manager
neovim      | neovim editor-tools|          |                     |                       | Neovim, with Vikix's config and its plugins
devtools    | lang-tools         |          |                     |                       | Tools for any language: ctags, entr, hyperfine, tokei, just, Zeal for offline docs
c           | lang-c             | devtools |                     |                       | C: clang, tcc, cmake, meson, rr, the C language server
python      | lang-python        | devtools |                     |                       | Python: uv, ruff, IPython, pytest, and JupyterLab in ~/dev/python
lisp        | lang-lisp          | devtools |                     |                       | More Lisps: Clozure CL, Racket, Chez Scheme, Guile, PicoLisp (SBCL is always here)
haskell     | lang-haskell       | devtools |                     |                       | Haskell: GHC, cabal, the language server, hlint
lua         | lang-lua           | devtools |                     |                       | Lua 5.4, LuaJIT, luarocks, the language server
go          | lang-go            | devtools |                     |                       | Go, the delve debugger, gopls
zig         | lang-zig           | devtools |                     |                       | Zig and zls
forth       | lang-forth         | devtools |                     |                       | Forth: Gforth
ruby        | lang-ruby          | devtools |                     |                       | Ruby, with ri for its docs
sql         | lang-sql           | devtools |                     |                       | SQL: SQLite, litecli, DB Browser for SQLite
wasm        | lang-wasm          | devtools |                     |                       | WebAssembly: wabt and wasmtime
javascript  | lang-javascript    | devtools |                     |                       | JavaScript, with Node
rust        | lang-rust          | devtools |                     |                       | Rust: cargo, rust-analyzer, the book offline
java        | lang-java          | devtools |                     |                       | Java: OpenJDK 21 and Gradle
ocaml       | lang-ocaml         | devtools |                     |                       | OCaml: dune, opam
julia       | lang-julia         | devtools |                     |                       | Julia, through juliaup
pascal      | lang-pascal        | devtools |                     |                       | Free Pascal and the Lazarus IDE
office      | office             |          |                     |                       | LibreOffice: documents, spreadsheets, presentations
printing    | printing           |          |                     |                       | Printers: CUPS, finding printers on the network, drivers
webapps     | optional/webapps   |          |                     |                       | Chromium, for web apps (vikix webapp add)
dropbox     | optional/dropbox   |          |                     |                       | Dropbox: ~/Dropbox kept in sync, and the bar shows what's left (dropbox start -i the first time)
video       | optional/video     |          |                     |                       | Video: Shotcut to edit, OBS to record with sound, HandBrake, yt-dlp
graphics    | optional/graphics  |          |                     |                       | Pictures: GIMP, Inkscape, Krita, darktable for RAW photos, Flameshot to mark up screenshots
blender     | optional/blender   |          |                     |                       | Blender: 3D, animation and its own video editor (230 MB)
study       | optional/study     |          |                     |                       | Study: Anki flashcards, and Xournal++ to write on PDFs
passwords   | optional/passwords |          |                     |                       | KeePassXC: passwords and two-factor codes, offline in a file of your own
bitwarden   | optional/bitwarden |          | vikix bitwarden setup | vikix bitwarden uninstall | Bitwarden: your passwords and two-factor codes from your Bitwarden account, typed into any window (Super+Shift+v)
phone       | optional/phone     |          |                     |                       | An Android phone's screen in a window (scrcpy, over adb)
wallpapers  |                    |          | vikix wallpapers setup | vikix wallpapers uninstall | Vid's wallpapers (about 40 MB): the wallpaper cycles through them, and they're in the Super+m picker; vikix update brings new ones
cli-extras  | optional/cli-extras|          |                     |                       | More terminal tools: pandoc converts documents, ncdu shows what fills the disk
windows     | optional/windows   |          | vikix windows setup | vikix windows remove  | Windows 11 in a window (8 GB of memory, 40 GB of disk)
local-ai    |                    |          | vikix ai setup      | vikix ai uninstall    | AI models on this laptop, with Ollama
llm         |                    |          | vikix ai llm        | uv tool uninstall llm | llm: AI on the command line, local or Claude
dictation   | optional/dictation |          | vikix dictate setup | vikix dictate uninstall | Dictation: speak, and it types what you said (Super+F9), on this laptop
lisp-apps   | optional/lisp-apps |          | vikix lisp-apps setup | vikix lisp-apps uninstall | Lisp programs, changeable in Lisp as StumpWM is: Nyxt (a browser), Lem (an editor), McCLIM's Listener
esploro     |                    | emacs    | vikix esploro setup | vikix esploro uninstall | Esploro: a file explorer in Emacs, with menus, the mouse, drag and drop and undo, that knows which window has each file open (Super+e)
hype        | optional/hype      |          | vikix hype setup    | vikix hype uninstall  | Hype: Markdown slides with a visual editor, in your theme's colours, export to PDF and PowerPoint
notes       | optional/notes     | local-ai | vikix notes setup   | vikix notes uninstall | Ask your notes from any terminal: note ask "...", from a folder of Markdown (an Obsidian vault), on this laptop
voice       |                    | dictation llm | vikix voice setup | vikix voice uninstall | Voice: talk to the AI and the agent, and they answer aloud (Super+F10, Super+F11)
opencode    |                    |          | vikix agent --install opencode | vikix agent --uninstall opencode | OpenCode: an AI agent for any model company, or local (vikix agent --use opencode)
codex       |                    |          | vikix agent --install codex | vikix agent --uninstall codex | Codex: OpenAI's AI agent, with your ChatGPT login, or local (vikix agent --use codex)
gemini      |                    | javascript | vikix agent --install gemini | vikix agent --uninstall gemini | Gemini CLI: Google's AI agent, with your Google login (vikix agent --use gemini)
aider       |                    |          | vikix agent --install aider | vikix agent --uninstall aider | Aider: an AI agent for your code, with an API key, or local (vikix agent --use aider)
